cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this toolkit or its provenance records, please cite the paper that presents it (preferred citation below)."
title: "5LTEP-L4: 5L-TEP Layer 4 Provenance Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of Layer 4 (Observability and Provenance) of the
  Five-Layer Trust Engineering Pyramid (5L-TEP, SOFTENG 2026) for open
  government data: every six hours it reads the metadata of every dataset of a
  CKAN portal, fingerprints it with SHA-256, classifies each change
  (CONTENT_MOD, SCHEMA_DRIFT, RETRO_ALTER), describes how the dataset changed
  (fields, relocations to another server, zip/plain packaging), and appends a
  W3C PROV-DM (JSON-LD) record to a per-dataset derivation chain with a
  dual-agent model (observer and data custodian). A daily independent
  cross-check, a static dashboard and status badges publish the results. One
  value (the portal URL in portal.json) adapts it to another CKAN portal.
